---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteExtras from '@/components/SiteExtras.astro';
import '@/styles/research-primer.css';
import { withBase } from '@/utils/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Inventory & Warranty" active="Research">
  <main class="site-shell research-primer-page">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="ui-copy-en">Research primer · 01</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">研究科普 · 01</span></div>
      <h1>Inventory & Warranty</h1>
      <p class="research-primer-lede">
        <span class="ui-copy-en">Warranty turns yesterday's sales and failures into tomorrow's service demand. The inventory problem is no longer only “how much should I order?”—it is also “what history do I need to remember in order to decide well?”</span>
        <span class="ui-copy-zh">保修会把过去的销售、产品年龄与失效，转化成未来的售后替换需求。因此问题不再只是“该订多少货”，还变成了“为了做对决策，我到底需要记住多少历史信息”。</span>
      </p>
      <div class="research-primer-meta">
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory control</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存控制</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Replacement warranty</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">替换保修</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Failure uncertainty</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">失效不确定性</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Sequential decisions</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">序贯决策</span></span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="primer-flow" aria-label="Inventory and warranty mental model">
      <div class="primer-flow-track" style="--flow-count:5">
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>01</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Units sold</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">产品售出</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>02</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Installed base ages</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">在保产品逐渐老化</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>03</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Failures occur</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">发生失效</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step is-focus"><b>04</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Replacement demand</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">产生替换需求</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>05</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory decision</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">做库存决策</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">What makes this different from ordinary inventory?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">它为什么不是一个普通库存问题？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">In ordinary textbook inventory models, demand is often treated as an external random process. Warranty service demand is partly generated by the firm's own past sales and the age of the installed base.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">很多经典库存模型把需求当作系统外部给定的随机过程；而保修需求却部分由企业过去卖出了多少产品、这些产品现在多大年龄共同“制造”出来。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-prose">
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Imagine selling a cohort of products today. Some of them may fail next month, some much later, and some never during the warranty period. Each covered failure may create a replacement request. The future service stream therefore carries a memory of earlier sales.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">可以想象今天卖出一批产品：其中一些下个月就会坏，一些很久以后才坏，还有一些在保修期内都不会坏。只要失效被保修覆盖，就可能形成替换需求。因此，未来的售后需求天然带着“过去销售历史的记忆”。</span></p>
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">That memory is the interesting part. If failure risk changes with product age, two systems with the same current inventory can face very different futures because their installed bases have different age compositions.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">真正有意思的是这份“记忆”。如果失效率随着产品年龄变化，那么两个系统即使当前库存完全相同，只要在保产品的年龄结构不同，它们面对的未来风险就可能截然不同。</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-concepts">
        <article class="primer-concept"><span>A</span><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Installed base</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">在保产品群体</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">The population of products still capable of generating warranty demand. Its age composition can be decision-relevant.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">仍可能产生保修需求的产品群体。它们的年龄构成往往直接影响未来替换需求。</span></p></article>
        <article class="primer-concept"><span>B</span><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Failure process</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">失效过程</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">A stochastic mechanism that converts installed products into service requests. Age dependence makes the process especially important.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">把在保产品随机转化成售后请求的机制；一旦失效率与年龄有关，状态表示就会更复杂。</span></p></article>
        <article class="primer-concept"><span>C</span><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Service inventory</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">售后备件库存</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Stock held to satisfy replacements quickly, balancing shortage risk against holding and replenishment costs.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">为了及时履行替换义务而持有的库存，需要在缺货风险、持有成本与补货成本之间平衡。</span></p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">A minimal mathematical picture</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">一个最小的数学图景</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">The exact model can become rich very quickly, but three relations already show where the difficulty comes from.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">具体模型可以很复杂，但只看三个最基本的关系，就已经能看到困难从哪里出现。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-equations">
        <div class="primer-equation"><code>I(t+1) = I(t) + Q(t) - R(t)</code><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory evolves through replenishment Q and replacement demand R.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">库存由补货 Q 与替换需求 R 共同推动。</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-equation"><code>R(t) = Σₐ F(t,a)</code><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Replacement demand can be viewed as failures aggregated across age cohorts a.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">替换需求可以理解为不同年龄组产品失效数量的汇总。</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-equation"><code>decision = f(inventory, installed-base information)</code><span><span class="ui-copy-en">The key modelling question is how much installed-base information the decision function really needs.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">关键问题是：做库存决策时，究竟需要保留多少关于在保产品群体的信息。</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">The research questions I care about</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">我真正关心的研究问题</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">For me, the most interesting part is not merely forecasting failures. It is understanding what failure uncertainty does to the decision problem itself.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">对我来说，最有意思的并不只是“预测会坏多少台”，而是失效不确定性究竟怎样改变了整个决策问题的结构。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-question-list">
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q1</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">What is a sufficient state?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">什么才是充分状态？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Do we need the complete age profile of the installed base, or can it be compressed into a smaller statistic without losing optimality?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">我们是否必须记录完整的年龄结构？还是存在更低维的统计量，既压缩信息又不损失最优性？</span></p></div></article>
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q2</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Does a simple policy structure survive?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">简单策略结构还能不能保留下来？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Classical inventory theory often gives base-stock or threshold policies. Warranty memory may preserve, weaken, or destroy those structures.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">经典库存理论常能得到基库存或阈值策略；加入保修记忆以后，这些结构可能保留、变弱，也可能彻底消失。</span></p></div></article>
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q3</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">When is approximation justified?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">什么时候应该做近似？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">If the exact state becomes high-dimensional, dynamic programming can become computationally expensive. Then approximation is not decoration—it becomes part of the modelling strategy.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">当精确状态维度过高时，动态规划会迅速变得昂贵。此时近似并不是“锦上添花”，而会成为建模方法本身的一部分。</span></p></div></article>
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q4</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">What information should data estimate?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">数据到底应该帮助我们估计什么？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Failure data can estimate reliability, but the operational value of an estimate depends on how it changes the replenishment decision.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">失效数据可以估计可靠性参数，但一个估计到底有没有运营价值，最终要看它是否真的改变库存决策。</span></p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">How this connects to the other two fields</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">它怎样和另外两个领域连起来？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Inventory & Warranty is the application domain. Stochastic Optimization supplies the sequential-decision machinery; Operations Research provides the broader modelling language.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">Inventory & Warranty 是具体问题场景；Stochastic Optimization 提供序贯决策工具；Operations Research 则提供更广义的建模与优化语言。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-related">
        <a href={withBase('/research/stochastic-optimization')}><small>02 · Next field</small><strong>Stochastic Optimization</strong><span><span class="ui-copy-en">State, uncertainty, Bellman logic, approximation.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">状态、不确定性、Bellman 逻辑与近似方法。</span></span></a>
        <a href={withBase('/research/operations-research')}><small>03 · Wider frame</small><strong>Operations Research</strong><span><span class="ui-copy-en">From a real system to a model, algorithm, and decision rule.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">从真实系统到模型、算法与可执行决策。</span></span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="research-primer-back">
      <a href={withBase('/research')}>← <span class="ui-copy-en">Back to Research</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">返回研究主页</span></a>
      <a href={withBase('/papers')}><span class="ui-copy-en">Continue with paper reading →</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">继续看论文阅读 →</span></a>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteExtras />
</BaseLayout>
